From 5a1d92cff1f525270f866c2a832ef1fbf0ea97ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: giteaguy <73799093+irnutsmurt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:18:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lifter: --traps, code excluded from the lift; the runtime
 traps it

A title's port may replace a whole library of the executable with code of
its own (an audio middleware with a native implementation, say) and must
then hold none of the library's implementation, not even unused, while any
path still reaching it shows itself.

ppu_lifter.py --traps FILE: {"traps": [{"lo", "hi", "what"}]}, half-open
guest ranges. Every function that starts in one is emitted as a call of
ppu_trap(addr, what, ctx) -- not one instruction of its body is in the
output, nor its fall-through chain -- and the ranges are registered with the
runtime (ppu_trap_ranges_register, from the function table's file). The
ranges must follow the lift's function boundaries: a lifted function that
runs into one, or a trapped one that runs out of it, is refused, as is an
entry hook, an instruction patch, an entry observer or --promote-calls
inside excluded code.

runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp: ppu_trap reports the address, the range's name,
the caller (lr, r3, the thread), the host chain and the guest's stack, then
ends the run (ps3_fatal). A lookup that finds no function (ppu_lookup's
miss) checks the ranges: an indirect call or a function pointer into the
middle of excluded code, or a thread or callback entering it, ends in the
same trap rather than as an unknown address. A lift from before --traps
compiles as before (PPU_RECOMP_HAS_TRAPS).

tools/test_ppu_traps.py (runtime/ppu/tests/test_ppu_traps.cpp): a made-up
program with two excluded functions, lifted, checked and built against the
real ppu_loader.cpp: neither body in the source; an entry hook in the range
and a function that runs into it refused; a direct call, an indirect call
through CTR, a function pointer read from guest memory, a tail call, a call
into the middle of an excluded function and a fall-through into one each end
the run at the trap naming the address reached; a call to a function not
excluded runs and returns. 16 checks, all pass (Windows, zig c++).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
